.TH SDL_RenderViewportSet 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_RenderViewportSet \- Return whether an explicit rectangle was set as the viewport.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_RenderViewportSet(SDL_Renderer *renderer);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is useful if you\(aqre saving and restoring the viewport and want to know whether you should restore a specific rectangle or NULL\[char46]
.PP
Each render target has its own viewport\[char46] This function checks the viewport for the current render target\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the viewport was set to a specific rectangle, or false if it was set to NULL (the entire target)\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

